USER def measure_spec_section4(root: Path) -> list[str]:
USER     """SECTION 4's FIELD TABLE, cell by cell against the base commit.
USER 
USER     This release changes no requirement, so the table that says what a record must carry moves in
USER     exactly one place: ``specVersion``'s example note, which names the release. Every other cell of
USER     every row — the field name, its type, whether it is required, and its notes — is the base
USER     commit's, compared as text. The required? cell is ALSO compared by its answer, so a flip from
USER     required to not-required is reported in the terms a reader cares about even when both cells are
USER     non-empty.
USER 
USER     Why the measurement is per cell and not a whole-row mask: the section-4 ``specVersion`` row is the
USER     one row a release may touch, and an earlier revision exempted the whole row. Masking the row
USER     masked its required cell too, so flipping `yes` to `no` — which turns a required field into an
USER     optional one, a requirement change — passed. It is the example note that moves; the row is not
USER     exempt.
USER 
USER     Red on: a row removed or added; a type, required or notes cell changed outside the example note;
USER     the example note left naming a version that is not the release; the example note's PROSE reworded
