USER # Evaluator Driven — the custody record
USER 
USER A specification for the record kept with a piece of evaluated work: what the work was measured against,
USER who measured it, what they found, and who decided. The record makes work answerable, not correct.
USER 
USER Why the name: see "Why this name" in `SPEC.md`.
USER 
USER **Who this is for**
USER - **Implementers** who want work they hand off, or receive, to carry its own account.
USER - **Reviewers** in procurement, security, or legal who need to check that account. Start with the
USER   [reviewer's guide](docs/REVIEWERS-GUIDE.md); every word the specification uses is in the
USER   [glossary](docs/GLOSSARY.md).
USER 
USER **Status: v0.9.8, candidate.** Early. One reference checker exists, in this repository. Known
USER implementations and their status are listed in the doctrine's README:
USER <https://github.com/evaluatordriven/doctrine#the-custody-record>. Nothing here implies endorsement by
USER anyone. Each release carries
USER its own custody record in `record/`, kept with that release's tag; this release's record claims CL1,
USER and states why not higher.
USER 
USER **Limits, stated first**
USER - The evidence base is one author's work and a handful of jobs.
USER - The reference checker verifies a record's shape and internal consistency. It cannot tell whether a
USER   reading was honest; that is what independent evaluators and the approver are for.
USER - External evidence (CL1-15, CL3-3) is only as good as the party who read it.
USER - No signing tool ships here yet, **by decision rather than omission**, and the reference checker does not
USER   verify signatures, so it reads CL3-3 as `NOT-CHECKABLE`: no record reaches CL3 with it. SPEC.md names
USER   Sigstore as the method; [`docs/SIGNING-DECISION.md`](docs/SIGNING-DECISION.md) records why it is not
USER   built, what was weighed instead, and the three conditions that would start it.
USER - The custody log catches an edited, removed or reordered event, but a log rewritten from the start, or
USER   cut short at the end, still verifies. Nothing outside the log anchors it until the record is signed.
USER - A control shows that a reader caught a known case. No checker can tell whether the case was hard enough
USER   to miss.
USER - "Held out" means held out from the maker of the record in hand, not from everyone.
USER - Records whose evidence files are withheld read `NOT-CHECKABLE` on CL1-8 and CL1-15 for anyone without
USER   those files. That includes this repository's own records: their reader evidence is private.
USER - This release had no reader panel, guide tester or human reader. Its record says so.
USER - There is no certifying body, assessor or registry. A record certifies nothing; see GOVERNANCE.md.
USER - One person maintains the specification. GOVERNANCE.md says how it continues without him.
USER 
USER ## Quickstart
USER 
USER Python 3.10 or newer, standard library only:
USER 
USER ```sh
USER git clone https://github.com/evaluatordriven/custody && cd custody
USER python3 tools/make_record.py examples/minimal/inputs.json examples/minimal/record.json
USER python3 checker/check.py examples/minimal/record.json --files examples/minimal --bar examples/minimal/bar.md --evidence examples/minimal/evidence
USER ```
USER 
USER The second command turns a hand-written inputs file into a record, computing every digest. The third
USER checks it against the work's files, the bar, and the evidence behind each reading, and prints a report;
USER exit code 0 means `OK`, 1 `FAILED`, 2 `NOT-CHECKABLE`. CI runs these two commands exactly.
USER 
USER To make your own: copy `examples/minimal/`, replace the files with yours, edit `inputs.json`, and run
USER the same two commands.
USER 
USER ## Record as you go
USER 
USER `tools/record.py` keeps a custody log while the work happens: each event gets the clock time and the
USER digests of the files it names, chained so that an edited, reordered or missing event is caught.
USER 
USER ```
USER python3 tools/record.py init job.jsonl --job "Q3 vendor report"
USER python3 tools/record.py add job.jsonl bar-frozen --actor "Casey Park" --file bar.md
USER python3 tools/make_record.py inputs.json record.json --log job.jsonl
USER ```
USER 
USER ## What is here
USER 
USER | Path | What it is |
USER |---|---|
USER | `SPEC.md` | The specification. Its *(normative)* sections define conformance. |
USER | `schema/custody-v1.schema.json` | The record's shape, for JSON Schema 2020-12 validators |
USER | `checker/check.py` | Reference verifier (not normative) |
USER | `tools/make_record.py` | Builds a record from a plain inputs file, or from a custody log (`--log`) |
