USER 
USER ## 8. Versioning *(normative)*
USER 
USER This specification follows Semantic Versioning 2.0.0. A record names the version it was written to in
USER `specVersion`. A change that would turn an `OK` record into a `FAILED` one is a major change; the
USER predicate type's version changes with the major version. Before 1.0.0, any release may make such a
USER change, and CHANGELOG.md lists it. An identifier renamed within a major version keeps its old value valid
USER until the next major version: `CL2-4` is not a requirement of its own; it is the former name of `CL1-15`,
USER accepted wherever `CL1-15` is. Each release is
USER a git tag and is citable by commit. No implementation is part of the specification.
USER 
